{"id":"903449d0d0b9a8c581ca5c6c07ec3ad05d9db0e0","axis":"silent","repo":"appwrite/appwrite","sha":"903449d0d0b9a8c581ca5c6c07ec3ad05d9db0e0","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/ci.yml","lines":["@@ -471,7 +471,7 @@ jobs:","             rustup component add clippy rustfmt &&","             cargo fmt --all --check &&","             cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings &&","-            cargo test --locked -p php-std -p utopia-image -p utopia-locale --all-features'","+            cargo test --locked -p php-std -p utopia-image -p utopia-locale -p utopia-user-agent --all-features'"," ","       - name: Build the image","         run: docker build --target development --tag appwrite-utopia --build-arg TESTING=true .","@@ -510,6 +510,19 @@ jobs:","             _APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES=locale php crates/extension/tests/locale.php > /tmp/rust.jsonl","             diff /tmp/php.jsonl /tmp/rust.jsonl'"," ","+      - name: Test UserAgent on the extension","+        run: |","+          # Utopia\\UserAgent\\UserAgent is registered only when _APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES names user-agent:","+          # the package's tests must pass on it, and the parity corpus must print the same on both.","+          docker run --rm --volume \"$PWD/packages:/usr/src/code/packages\" \\","+            --volume \"$PWD/crates:/usr/src/code/crates\" appwrite-utopia sh -c '","+            set -e","+            _APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES=user-agent php -r \"exit((new ReflectionClass(Utopia\\\\UserAgent\\\\UserAgent::class))->isInternal() ? 0 : 1);\"","+            _APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES=user-agent vendor/bin/phpunit --no-configuration --bootstrap vendor/autoload.php packages/user-agent/tests","+            php crates/extension/tests/user-agent.php > /tmp/php.jsonl","+            _APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES=user-agent php crates/extension/tests/user-agent.php > /tmp/rust.jsonl","+            diff /tmp/php.jsonl /tmp/rust.jsonl'","+","   build:","     name: Build","     needs: changes"],"additions":14,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"Cargo.lock","lines":["@@ -2540,6 +2540,7 @@ dependencies = [","  \"utopia-dsn\",","  \"utopia-image\",","  \"utopia-locale\",","+ \"utopia-user-agent\","," ]"," "," [[package]]","@@ -2572,6 +2573,15 @@ dependencies = [","  \"thiserror 2.0.21\","," ]"," ","+[[package]]","+name = \"utopia-user-agent\"","+version = \"0.1.0\"","+dependencies = [","+ \"aho-corasick\",","+ \"memchr\",","+ \"php-std\",","+]","+"," [[package]]"," name = \"v_frame\""," version = \"0.3.9\""],"additions":10,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -25,11 +25,14 @@ php-std = { path = \"crates/support/php-std\" }"," utopia-dsn = { path = \"crates/utopia/dsn\" }"," utopia-image = { path = \"crates/utopia/image\", default-features = false }"," utopia-locale = { path = \"crates/utopia/locale\" }","+utopia-user-agent = { path = \"crates/utopia/user-agent\" }"," "," # #[php(sensitive(...))] (extphprs/ext-php-rs#840), which `Utopia\\DSN\\DSN` needs to keep"," # credentials out of exception traces: the PR's commit, which GitHub serves from the upstream"," # repository. Back to a release once it ships in one."," ext-php-rs = { git = \"https://github.com/extphprs/ext-php-rs\", rev = \"fb34246728d501d81b44348f679c7538f3d1d16a\" }","+# Multi-needle substring search (utopia-user-agent: the bot table, in one pass).","+aho-corasick = \"1\""," argon2 = { version = \"0.5\", features = [\"std\"] }"," blowfish = { version = \"0.9\", features = [\"bcrypt\"] }"," bytes = \"1\"","@@ -43,6 +46,8 @@ icu_properties = { version = \"2.3\", default-features = false, features = [\"compi"," indexmap = \"2\""," md-5 = \"0.10\""," md2 = \"0.10\"","+# Byte search (utopia-user-agent: case-insensitive token scans); pure Rust.","+memchr = \"2\""," ripemd = \"0.1\""," rustix = { version = \"1\", default-features = false, features = [\"std\", \"fs\", \"system\"] }"," ryu = \"1\""],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -21,3 +21,4 @@ php-std.workspace = true"," utopia-dsn.workspace = true"," utopia-image = { workspace = true, features = [\"libwebp\", \"libheif\"] }"," utopia-locale.workspace = true","+utopia-user-agent.workspace = true"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/README.md","lines":["@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ implementation of them. Every other class is registered only when `_APP_EXTENSIO"," its package. Otherwise Composer loads the package's PHP class as before:"," "," ```sh","-_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES=dsn,locale   # Utopia\\DSN\\DSN and Utopia\\Locale\\Locale from the extension","+_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES=dsn,locale,user-agent   # Utopia\\DSN\\DSN, Utopia\\Locale\\Locale and Utopia\\UserAgent\\UserAgent from the extension"," ```"," "," The extension reads it once, when PHP loads the module, so changing it takes a restart and no","@@ -81,6 +81,25 @@ each case raises. It asserts these known differences on the extension:"," A warning PHP raises inside the class (`file_get_contents()` of a missing file) names the caller's"," file and line, since the class has no PHP source."," ","+## Utopia\\UserAgent\\UserAgent","+","+Over `crates/utopia/user-agent` (`_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES=user-agent`). Only `UserAgent` moves: what","+it returns are the package's own `OperatingSystem`, `Client`, `Device` and `Bot` objects, built by","+their PHP constructors once per agent and returned as the same object on every call, as in PHP. The","+detectors in `Utopia\\UserAgent\\Detection` stay PHP. The class is final with a private constructor","+and the PHP class's private properties, so `==`, `var_dump()` and `(array)` see what they see in PHP.","+","+`crates/extension/tests/user-agent.php` prints a corpus of results that must be identical on both","+implementations: every string in the package's tests, agents Appwrite sees (SDKs, the CLI, HTTP","+libraries, browsers, previews, monitors, bots), edge cases (empty, case, control bytes, bytes that are","+not UTF-8, 100 KB inputs) and seeded mutations of all of them, read through every method and through","+`Appwrite\\Detector\\Detector`. It asserts these known differences on the extension:","+","+- A `null`, array or object argument and a missing argument raise the same `TypeError` and","+  `ArgumentCountError` with ext-php-rs's message.","+- `isset()` on a private property from outside the class is `true`.","+- `serialize()` refuses the object, as it does every class with Rust state.","+"," ## Benchmarks"," "," Every class's PR carries a benchmark against the PHP class. `crates/extension/bench/<name>.php`"],"additions":20,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/bench/user-agent.php","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@","+<?php","+","+// Times Utopia\\UserAgent\\UserAgent on whichever implementation loaded. Compare both with","+// `python3 crates/extension/bench/run.py crates/extension/bench/user-agent.php . <utopia.so> 5`.","+","+require __DIR__ . '/../../../vendor/autoload.php';","+","+use Appwrite\\Detector\\Detector;","+use Utopia\\UserAgent\\UserAgent;","+","+// A run meant for the extension that gets the PHP class would time PHP against PHP.","+$internal = (new ReflectionClass(UserAgent::class))->isInternal();","+$requested = in_array('user-agent', array_map(trim(...), explode(',', getenv('_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES') ?: '')), true);","+if ($internal !== $requested) {","+    fwrite(STDERR, '_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES ' . ($requested ? 'names' : 'does not name') . ' user-agent, but the other implementation loaded' . PHP_EOL);","+    exit(1);","+}","+","+// What a session or usage event does: the OS, client and device of one agent, through Appwrite's Detector.","+$detect = function (string $agent): void {","+    $detector = new Detector($agent);","+    $detector->getOS();","+    $detector->getClient();","+    $detector->getDevice();","+};","+$chrome = 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/126.0.0.0 Safari/537.36';","+$iphone = 'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 17_4 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/17.4 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1';","+$android = 'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 14; SM-S918B) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/126.0.6478.71 Mobile Safari/537.36';","+$sdk = 'AppwriteNodeJSSDK/14.1.0 (Linux; x64)';","+$googlebot = 'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Googlebot/2.1; +http://www.google.com/bot.html)';","+$gptbot = 'Mozilla/5.0 AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko; compatible; GPTBot/1.2; +https://openai.com/gptbot)';","+$uptime = 'Mozilla/5.0+(compatible; UptimeRobot/2.0; http://www.uptimerobot.com/)';","+$crawler = 'AcmeCrawler/1.0 (+https://acme.example/crawler)';","+$cases = [","+    'Detector desktop Chrome' => fn () => $detect($chrome),","+    'Detector iPhone Safari' => fn () => $detect($iphone),","+    'Detector Android Chrome' => fn () => $detect($android),","+    'Detector SDK' => fn () => $detect($sdk),","+    'isBot browser' => fn () => UserAgent::parse($chrome)->isBot(),","+    'isBot Googlebot' => fn () => UserAgent::parse($googlebot)->isBot(),","+    'isBot GPTBot' => fn () => UserAgent::parse($gptbot)->isBot(),","+    'isBot UptimeRobot' => fn () => UserAgent::parse($uptime)->isBot(),","+    'isBot generic crawler' => fn () => UserAgent::parse($crawler)->isBot(),","+    'toArray Android Chrome' => fn () => UserAgent::parse($android)->toArray(),","+];","+$n = 20000;","+$out = [];","+foreach ($cases as $name => $fn) {","+    for ($i = 0; $i < 500; $i++) {","+        $fn();","+    }","+    $runs = [];","+    for ($r = 0; $r < 5; $r++) {","+        $t = hrtime(true);","+        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {","+            $fn();","+        }","+        $runs[] = (hrtime(true) - $t) / $n;","+    }","+    sort($runs);","+    $out[$name] = $runs[2];","+}","+$out['peak memory MB'] = round(memory_get_peak_usage(true) / 1048576, 1);","+echo json_encode($out), \"\\n\";"],"additions":64,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -5,13 +5,14 @@"," //! `Utopia\\Image\\Canvas` and `Utopia\\Image\\Font` are always registered: their"," //! package has no PHP implementation. Every other library still has one, and"," //! its class is registered only when `_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES` names its","-//! package (`dsn`, `locale`), so each can be canaried and switched back to PHP with a","+//! package (`dsn`, `locale`, `user-agent`), so each can be canaried and switched back to PHP with a"," //! restart, not a deploy."," "," mod canvas;"," mod dsn;"," mod locale;"," mod string;","+mod user_agent;"," "," use ext_php_rs::prelude::*;"," ","@@ -29,9 +30,13 @@ fn enabled(package: &str) -> bool {"," pub fn get_module(module: ModuleBuilder) -> ModuleBuilder {","     let module = module.name(\"utopia\").class::<canvas::Canvas>().class::<canvas::Font>();","     let module = if enabled(\"dsn\") { module.class::<dsn::Dsn>() } else { module };","-    if enabled(\"locale\") {","-        module.class::<locale::Locale>().request_shutdown_function(locale::request_shutdown)","-    } else {","-        module","-    }","+    let module = if enabled(\"locale\") { module.class::<locale::Locale>() } else { module };","+    let module = if enabled(\"user-agent\") { module.class::<user_agent::UserAgent>() } else { module };","+    module.request_shutdown_function(request_shutdown)","+}","+","+/// Forgets what the classes hold for the request when it ends, as PHP frees its static state.","+extern \"C\" fn request_shutdown(kind: i32, module: i32) -> i32 {","+    user_agent::request_shutdown();","+    locale::request_shutdown(kind, module)"," }"],"additions":11,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/src/locale.rs","lines":["@@ -197,7 +197,7 @@ impl ext_php_rs::convert::StubLiteral for Placeholders<'_> {"," }"," "," /// A property value of any type, shared by refcount.","-pub struct Value(Zval);","+pub struct Value(pub Zval);"," "," impl ext_php_rs::convert::IntoZval for Value {","     const TYPE: ext_php_rs::flags::DataType = ext_php_rs::flags::DataType::Mixed;"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/src/user_agent.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,248 @@","+//! `Utopia\\UserAgent\\UserAgent` over [`utopia_user_agent`]. What it returns are the","+//! package's own PHP value objects (`OperatingSystem`, `Client`, `Device`, `Bot`),","+//! built once per agent and returned as the same object on every call, as PHP does.","+//! Their class entries are looked up once per request.","+","+use std::cell::Cell;","+","+use ext_php_rs::boxed::ZBox;","+use ext_php_rs::convert::IntoZval;","+use ext_php_rs::exception::PhpException;","+use ext_php_rs::flags::ClassFlags;","+use ext_php_rs::prelude::*;","+use ext_php_rs::types::{ZendHashTable, ZendStr, Zval};","+use ext_php_rs::zend::{ClassEntry, ce};","+use utopia_user_agent::{Text, detection};","+","+use crate::locale::Value;","+use crate::string::PhpString;","+","+/// `Utopia\\UserAgent\\UserAgent`: the string and each category once detected. Its","+/// private properties are the PHP class's, so `==`, `var_dump()` and `(array)` match.","+#[php_class]","+#[php(name = \"Utopia\\\\UserAgent\\\\UserAgent\", flags = ClassFlags::Final)]","+pub struct UserAgent {","+    value: Zval,","+    operating_system: Zval,","+    client: Zval,","+    device: Zval,","+    bot: Zval,","+    bot_resolved: bool,","+}","+","+impl Clone for UserAgent {","+    fn clone(&self) -> Self {","+        Self {","+            value: self.value.shallow_clone(),","+            operating_system: self.operating_system.shallow_clone(),","+            client: self.client.shallow_clone(),","+            device: self.device.shallow_clone(),","+            bot: self.bot.shallow_clone(),","+            bot_resolved: self.bot_resolved,","+        }","+    }","+}","+","+/// A PHP string of `bytes`, or `null`.","+fn text(value: Option<&[u8]>) -> Zval {","+    let mut zval = Zval::new();","+    match value {","+        Some(bytes) => zval.set_zend_string(ZendStr::new(bytes, false)),","+        None => zval.set_null(),","+    }","+    zval","+}","+","+/// The package's value classes, in the order of [`CLASSES`].","+const NAMES: [&str; 4] = [","+    \"Utopia\\\\UserAgent\\\\OperatingSystem\",","+    \"Utopia\\\\UserAgent\\\\Client\",","+    \"Utopia\\\\UserAgent\\\\Device\",","+    \"Utopia\\\\UserAgent\\\\Bot\",","+];","+const OPERATING_SYSTEM: usize = 0;","+const CLIENT: usize = 1;","+const DEVICE: usize = 2;","+const BOT: usize = 3;","+","+thread_local! {","+    /// The class entry of each of [`NAMES`] once found this request.","+    static CLASSES: [Cell<*const ClassEntry>; 4] = const { [const { Cell::new(std::ptr::null()) }; 4] };","+}","+","+/// Forgets the class entries at the end of a request, when PHP frees user classes.","+pub fn request_shutdown() {","+    CLASSES.with(|classes| classes.iter().for_each(|class| class.set(std::ptr::null())));","+}","+","+/// The class entry of `NAMES[index]`, autoloading it as PHP does on first use.","+fn class(index: usize) -> PhpResult<&'static ClassEntry> {","+    let cached = CLASSES.with(|classes| classes[index].get());","+    // SAFETY: a user class entry lives until the request ends, when the pointer is forgotten.","+    if let Some(entry) = unsafe { cached.as_ref() } {","+        return Ok(entry);","+    }","+    let name = NAMES[index];","+    let entry = ClassEntry::try_find(name)","+        .ok_or_else(|| PhpException::new(format!(\"Class \\\"{name}\\\" not found\"), 0, ce::error()))?;","+    CLASSES.with(|classes| classes[index].set(entry));","+    Ok(entry)","+}","+","+/// `new $class(...$arguments)` for the class `NAMES[index]`, calling its constructor","+/// as `new` does: by the class's constructor pointer, not by name.","+fn object<const N: usize>(index: usize, arguments: [Option<&Text<'_>>; N]) -> PhpResult<Zval> {","+    let entry = class(index)?;","+    let mut object = entry.new();","+    let mut arguments = arguments.map(|argument| text(argument.map(AsRef::as_ref)));","+    if !entry.constructor.is_null() {","+        let mut result = Zval::new();","+        // SAFETY: the constructor is the class's own, called on a new object of that class","+        // with initialized arguments that outlive the call, as the `NEW` opcode does.","+        unsafe {","+            ext_php_rs::ffi::zend_call_known_function(","+                entry.constructor,","+                std::ptr::from_mut(&mut *object),","+                std::ptr::from_ref(entry).cast_mut(),","+                &raw mut result,","+                N as u32,","+                arguments.as_mut_ptr(),","+                std::ptr::null_mut(),","+            );","+        }","+    }","+    object.into_zval(false).map_err(PhpException::from)","+}","+","+/// Calls `$value->toArray()`, or gives `null` for `null`.","+fn fields(value: &Zval) -> PhpResult<Zval> {","+    match value.object() {","+        Some(object) => object.try_call_method(\"toArray\", vec![]).map_err(PhpException::from),","+        None => Ok(Zval::null()),","+    }","+}","+","+impl UserAgent {","+    fn bytes(&self) -> &[u8] {","+        self.value.zend_str().map_or(&[], ZendStr::as_bytes)","+    }","+}","+","+#[php_impl]","+impl UserAgent {","+    /// The private properties of `UserAgent.php`, in its declaration order.","+    #[php(getter, name = \"operatingSystem\", vis = \"private\")]","+    pub fn operating_system_property(&self) -> Value {","+        Value(self.operating_system.shallow_clone())","+    }","+","+    #[php(getter, name = \"client\", vis = \"private\")]","+    pub fn client_property(&self) -> Value {","+        Value(self.client.shallow_clone())","+    }","+","+    #[php(getter, name = \"device\", vis = \"private\")]","+    pub fn device_property(&self) -> Value {","+        Value(self.device.shallow_clone())","+    }","+","+    #[php(getter, name = \"bot\", vis = \"private\")]","+    pub fn bot_property(&self) -> Value {","+        Value(self.bot.shallow_clone())","+    }","+","+    #[php(getter, name = \"botResolved\", vis = \"private\")]","+    pub fn bot_resolved_property(&self) -> bool {","+        self.bot_resolved","+    }","+","+    #[php(getter, name = \"value\", vis = \"private\")]","+    pub fn value_property(&self) -> Value {","+        Value(self.value.shallow_clone())","+    }","+","+    #[php(vis = \"private\")]","+    pub fn __construct(value: PhpString<'_>) -> Self {","+        Self::parse(value)","+    }","+","+    pub fn parse(value: PhpString<'_>) -> Self {","+        Self {","+            value: text(Some(value.bytes())),","+            operating_system: Zval::null(),","+            client: Zval::null(),","+            device: Zval::null(),","+            bot: Zval::null(),","+            bot_resolved: false,","+        }","+    }","+","+    pub fn raw(&self) -> Value {","+        Value(self.value.shallow_clone())","+    }","+","+    #[php(name = \"operatingSystem\")]","+    pub fn operating_system(&mut self) -> PhpResult<Value> {","+        if self.operating_system.is_null() {","+            let found = detection::operating_system(self.bytes());","+            self.operating_system =","+                object(OPERATING_SYSTEM, [found.code.as_ref(), found.name.as_ref(), found.version.as_ref()])?;","+        }","+        Ok(Value(self.operating_system.shallow_clone()))","+    }","+","+    pub fn client(&mut self) -> PhpResult<Value> {","+        if self.client.is_null() {","+            let found = detection::client(self.bytes());","+            self.client = object(","+                CLIENT,","+                [","+                    found.kind.as_ref(),","+                    found.code.as_ref(),","+                    found.name.as_ref(),","+                    found.version.as_ref(),","+                    found.engine.as_ref(),","+                    found.engine_version.as_ref(),","+                ],","+            )?;","+        }","+        Ok(Value(self.client.shallow_clone()))","+    }","+","+    pub fn device(&mut self) -> PhpResult<Value> {","+        if self.device.is_null() {","+            let found = detection::device(self.bytes());","+            self.device = object(DEVICE, [found.kind.as_ref(), found.brand.as_ref(), found.model.as_ref()])?;","+        }","+        Ok(Value(self.device.shallow_clone()))","+    }","+","+    pub fn bot(&mut self) -> PhpResult<Value> {","+        if !self.bot_resolved {","+            if let Some(found) = detection::bot(self.bytes()) {","+                self.bot = object(BOT, [Some(&found.name), Some(&found.category)])?;","+            }","+            self.bot_resolved = true;","+        }","+        Ok(Value(self.bot.shallow_clone()))","+    }","+","+    #[php(name = \"isBot\")]","+    pub fn is_bot(&mut self) -> PhpResult<bool> {","+        Ok(self.bot()?.0.is_object())","+    }","+","+    #[php(name = \"toArray\")]","+    pub fn array(&mut self) -> PhpResult<ZBox<ZendHashTable>> {","+        let mut result = ZendHashTable::new();","+        let os = self.operating_system()?;","+        result.insert(\"os\", fields(&os.0)?)?;","+        let client = self.client()?;","+        result.insert(\"client\", fields(&client.0)?)?;","+        let device = self.device()?;","+        result.insert(\"device\", fields(&device.0)?)?;","+        let bot = self.bot()?;","+        result.insert(\"bot\", fields(&bot.0)?)?;","+        Ok(result)","+    }","+}"],"additions":248,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/tests/user-agent.php","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,352 @@","+<?php","+","+// Parity corpus for Utopia\\UserAgent\\UserAgent. Run it on the PHP class and on the utopia","+// extension's (_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES=user-agent), and diff stdout: every line must match.","+// Stderr names the implementation that ran.","+","+require __DIR__ . '/../../../vendor/autoload.php';","+","+use Utopia\\UserAgent\\UserAgent;","+","+$internal = (new ReflectionClass(UserAgent::class))->isInternal();","+fwrite(STDERR, 'Utopia\\\\UserAgent\\\\UserAgent: ' . ($internal ? 'utopia extension' : 'PHP') . PHP_EOL);","+// A run meant for the extension that gets the PHP class would compare PHP with PHP and pass.","+$requested = in_array('user-agent', array_map(trim(...), explode(',', getenv('_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES') ?: '')), true);","+if ($internal !== $requested) {","+    fwrite(STDERR, '_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES ' . ($requested ? 'names' : 'does not name') . ' user-agent, but the other implementation loaded' . PHP_EOL);","+    exit(1);","+}","+","+/** Warnings raised by the current case. */","+$warnings = [];","+set_error_handler(function (int $level, string $message) use (&$warnings): bool {","+    $warnings[] = $message;","+","+    return true;","+});","+","+/** $value with every string that is not UTF-8 as its hex, so json_encode() cannot hide a byte. */","+function exported(mixed $value): mixed","+{","+    if (is_string($value)) {","+        return mb_check_encoding($value, 'UTF-8') ? $value : ['hex' => bin2hex($value)];","+    }","+    if (is_array($value)) {","+        return array_map(exported(...), $value);","+    }","+    if (is_object($value)) {","+        return ['class' => $value::class, 'properties' => exported(get_object_vars($value))];","+    }","+","+    return $value;","+}","+","+/** The observable outcome of $run: its value or exception, and the warnings it raised. */","+function outcome(callable $run): array","+{","+    global $warnings;","+    $warnings = [];","+    try {","+        $result = ['value' => exported($run())];","+    } catch (Throwable $e) {","+        $result = ['throws' => $e::class, 'message' => $e->getMessage()];","+    }","+    if ($warnings !== []) {","+        $result['warnings'] = $warnings;","+    }","+","+    return $result;","+}","+","+function emit(string $case, array $result): void","+{","+    echo json_encode([exported($case), $result], JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES | JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICO